<title>UK: UK's Camelot H1 sales, profits dip.</title>
<headline>UK's Camelot H1 sales, profits dip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>24 weeks to September 14, 1996</p>
<p>					 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Total sales		 2,096		  vs 2,510</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	    31.5		   vs 36.2</p>
<p> Cost of prizes	    1,058		  vs 1,271</p>
<p> Lottery duty		251.5		  vs 301.2</p>
<p> Money to Good Causes    567.8		  vs 678.8</p>
<p> Retailers' commission   107.0		  vs 128.3</p>
<p> Terminal and data costs  41.7		  vs 46.0</p>
<p> Gross profit		 69.8		  vs 84.4</p>
<p> Operating costs	    44.0		  vs 52.4</p>
<p> Other operating income   0.3		   vs  0.5</p>
<p> Operating profit	   26.1		  vs 32.5</p>
<p> Interest receivable	5.4		   vs  3.7</p>
<p> Tax paid		     10.7		  vs 12.6</p>
<p> Profit after tax	   20.8		  vs 23.6</p>
<p> Total dividend payment   10.0		  vs 9.5</p>
<p> Retained profit	    10.8		  vs 14.1</p>
<p>NOTE - UK lottery operator Camelot is owned by Cadbury Schweppes Plc, De La Rue Plc, GTECH UK limited, Racal Electronics Plc and Fujitsu Ltd unit ICL. The first four have 22.5 percent each, ICL 10 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
